  "notes": {
    "build": "Both custom binaries were built through their corresponding run.py build helper with clang -std=c11 -O2 -g -Wall -Wextra -Werror. Temporary binaries live under /tmp.",
    "interpretation": "CPU samples point to more work in compact allocate path and descriptor metadata. Descriptor-key hashing alone accounts for ~5-7% of sampled CPU. The sample percentages are attribution, not wall time. Compact allocate takes 58.63%/53.28% samples (ephemeral/atomic) versus baseline 32.21%/41.32%; store remains 17.78%/31.07% versus 21.36%/32.14%.",
    "attribution": "perf annotate with DWARF resolves allocate to current gc.c:314-334, descriptor_info/hash to 135-154, store to 336-348. Current per-allocation calls descriptor_info, and store decodes descriptor from the header each time.",
    "limitations": "One process/profile per binary at 500M, no repeated perf captures; timings are not used as claims. Existing correctness/sanitizer marker passed in all four artifacts.",
    "alignment_interpretation": "Report both nursery capacities. Compact ephemeral object stride is 32 B; 262144 holds 8192 objects (32 x 256) and is a favorable exact batch phase, while 262136 holds 8191 and shifts collection into a live batch. In copied-byte fractions, copied_bytes includes headers; copied_payload_bytes counts only payload. Do not treat the aligned case as representative.",
    "source_attribution": "perf annotate/DWARF maps the current allocation path to gc.c:314-334, descriptor_info/hash to 135-154, and store to 336-348. Flat symbol shares: allocate 58.63%/53.28%, store 17.78%/31.07% (ephemeral/atomic). The inlined descriptor_key path is a subset of allocate samples, about 6.74%/4.86% of total samples; it is not an additional share. These are CPU sample percentages, not absolute costs or wall-time comparisons."
